        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Textile panel of embroidered linen canvas with silk, gold and silver threads in cross stitch. Embroidered square with a cross shape depicting an elephant (right side view) standing in water on the edge is a partially embroidered jungle (tree on left is half-finished) against a blue sky background. There is a banner inscription which curls around, reading 'ELEPHANT'.  Behind the cross in the corners, are two birds in flight and two flower sprigs on green grass. Originally all the panels were applied to a green velvet background, and parts of which survive on the central panel and on several of the smaller panels."@en ;
